# The Crucial Difference

- `flex: 1` (`flex: 1 1 0%`) – items start from zero size and share all space equally. Great for equal‑width columns.
- `flex: auto` (`flex: 1 1 auto`) – items start at their natural size, then share **extra** space proportionally. If you want items to grow but respect their content, use `auto`.

Example:
```css
/* All columns exactly equal width */
.col { flex: 1; }

/* Columns grow from content size, sharing extra space */
.col { flex: auto; }
```

At a glance:
```css
/* Equal columns */
.equal { flex: 1; }

/* Fixed 300px, never shrink, but can grow if extra space */
.sidebar { flex: 1 0 300px; }

/* Only grow if space, don't shrink below content */
.label { flex: 0 0 auto; }
```
